From 2192f6a750b83e323f663486b1f5ddaa68e512e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 04:49:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sprint 8b: relabel diagnostics as 'Entering Grade N+1'
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Content tested stays the same (grade 6-11 material), but the picker
cards, page headers, and homepage grid now advertise them as
'Entering Grade 7' through 'Entering Grade 12'. This matches how a
parent thinks about back-to-school placement — a rising 7th grader
takes the grade-6 content test, not a grade-7 test they haven't
seen yet.

- Picker: 'Which grade is your student entering?' + card labels
  'Entering Grade N+1' with 'Grade N content' pill above
- Grade-specific pages: headline 'Entering Grade N+1 Diagnostic',
  scope box labeled 'Grade N content covered', copy notes each test
  is also valid as a mid-year check for current grade-N students
- Homepage: pill above each card reads 'Entering', big number is
  N+1, subtitle shows 'Grade N · <scope>'
- DiagnosticFlow default headline matches the new pattern
